Z||000005||Slammed Fiero||12-14-2000||02:41 PM||||I forget the website URL , but email<P>pyork@sympatico.ca<P><BR>he owns a place called mach1 motorsports and is a good friend of mine. Fiero LIsa is getting her wheels through him . 17"5zigen wheels with Kuhomo tires delievered for $1050. Nice wheels , he gets good deals and gets stuff cheaper than 99% of the places out there because he has no overhead...<P><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...||||reg||1
Z||000006||Jackalrr||12-14-2000||09:08 PM||||Go with 16" TSW BLADE! I just got mine on clearence for 50% off... that is $75 per rim.  I got them with premounted tires and all install stuff and shipping for only $808.00! What a deal.. I think...<P>They are out of 17" and will not be getting anymore.. but the 16"s really do look good.<P>-Charlie<BR>-----<BR>jackalrr@cinci.rr.com||||reg||1
Z||000007||william_thorniii||12-14-2000||09:26 PM||||jack,<P>Thanks for your advice.  I love TSW wheel center treatment and wish that they still made a decent style of rim.  Blades do look unbelieveable on Fieros.  <P>Unfortunately I like being different and since Archie started using Blades they are too common for my tastes.  I would like 18's at least out back, but will most likely settle for 17's seeing as I can get them for around $1000 with tires.  16's have too much sidewall for what the project I am working on.  I want to minimize tire roll-over.<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||14
